				"⣿⡏⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				235
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Expose ICodeEditorService on workbench accessor for extension decorations\n\nAdd ICodeEditorService to the CELExposeAccessor services facade so extensions' `createTextEditorDecorationType` and `setDecorationsByType` calls paint visible decorations (squiggles, gutter icons, inline hints) instead of silently no-oping.\n\nWithout this, every extension using the editor decoration API — including error squiggles from language servers — produces no visible result because the Sky bridge had no reference to the live Monaco editor service. Both `CodeEditor` and `CodeEditorService` keys expose the same ICodeEditorService instance, matching both the existing `Services.CodeEditorService.listCodeEditors()` call site and the new `Services.CodeEditor.registerDecorationType(...)` usage.\n\nRegenerate the full Configuration/ compiled output tree from the updated source, and standardise shell script indentation in Run.sh and prepublishOnly.sh to match the project's 2-space convention.",
			"SHA": "463cc2596550df59a1af7c488a10bd06666a8cff"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T13:48:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⣿⡇⠀",
				336,
				236
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Always apply MacTitlebarOffset and PartZIndex CSS fixes\n\nRemove the `LandDisableUIFixes` conditional gating from `InjectMacTitlebarOffsetCSS` and `InjectPartZIndexCSS` in both the main Pipeline and the BuildPipeline plugin index. These CSS injections are structural layout fixes — not performance optimisations — and should always execute regardless of the `DisableUIFixes` flag.\n\nClean up the entire `Configuration/` output tree by deleting stale compiled `.js` and `.js.map` artefacts alongside the source changes, and standardise case-statement indentation in `Run.sh` and `prepublishOnly.sh` for consistency.\n\nThe overhauled output tree now reflects only the currently-defined plugins, eliminating dead transforms from prior pipeline iterations.",
			"SHA": "c055befeb969dd3138690e857f6f80289aaa3a60"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T07:30:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Expose terminal service in Accessor module\n\nAdd ITerminalService to the Expose/Accessor module to enable terminal-related functionality. This change modifies both the TypeScript source and the compiled JavaScript output.\n\nThe update includes the necessary import and instantiation of the terminal service for integration with the service accessor.",
			"SHA": "0f1675dcac4a6442fb7c0e57080f601d6007f084"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T06:49:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				2
			],
			"Message": "style(Output): standardize indentation in shell scripts with spaces\n\nStandardize shell script formatting in build scripts `Run.sh` and `prepublishOnly.sh` to use 2-space indentation and consistent comment style. This aligns with hermes-shell-hooks linting and shellscript-maintenance standards. The changes ensure all scripts under the Output module use spaces for indentation and have re-formatted shell-style comments.",
			"SHA": "745639f2b7689c926755bb293fef1a78d44d923e"
		}
